
🧠 DFDL Data Types — Short Notes

🔹 1. Base Concept

DFDL apne data types define nahi karta.

Ye XML Schema (XSD) ke data types ka subset use karta.

DFDL ka role: Physical data (binary/text) → Logical model (XSD type) → Message tree (ESQL type)



---

🔹 2. Data Type Flow (IBM IIB / ACE)

Layer	Description

Physical Data	File, binary, CSV, COBOL, etc.
DFDL Parser	Converts physical → logical (XSD types)
Message Tree	Logical → ESQL types (for flows, mapping, compute nodes)



---

🔹 3. Common Type Mappings

Source (COBOL/Text)	DFDL Logical Type	XML Schema Type	IIB/ESQL Type

PIC 9(19)	Integer	xs:nonNegativeInteger	DECIMAL
Text Name	String	xs:string	CHARACTER
Amount (12.34)	Decimal	xs:decimal	DECIMAL
Date (2025-09-17)	Date	xs:date	DATE
Boolean (Y/N)	Boolean	xs:boolean	BOOLEAN



---

🔹 4. Automatic Casting (Supported)

Only from xs:string → Serializer can auto-convert CHARACTER → text field.

Useful for simple CSV / text-based DFDL parsing.



---

🔹 5. Unsupported Types ❌

Type	Why Problem

INTERVAL	No DFDL equivalent
BIT	Not mapped to XML Schema types


🧩 Error Example:
BIPxxxx: Serialization error: ESQL type INTERVAL not supported in DFDL schema


---

🔹 6. Example (CSV → XML Tree)

Input:

1001, Pankaj, 5000.75, 2025-09-17

Schema:

<xs:element name="Employee">
  <xs:complexType>
    <xs:sequence dfdl:separator="," dfdl:terminator="%NL;">
      <xs:element name="Id" type="xs:int"/>
      <xs:element name="Name" type="xs:string"/>
      <xs:element name="Salary" type="xs:decimal"/>
      <xs:element name="JoinDate" type="xs:date"/>
    </xs:sequence>
  </xs:complexType>
</xs:element>

Parsed Message Tree:

Employee
 ├── Id        = 1001        (INTEGER)
 ├── Name      = "Pankaj"    (CHARACTER)
 ├── Salary    = 5000.75     (DECIMAL)
 └── JoinDate  = 2025-09-17  (DATE)


---

🔹 7. Key Takeaways 💡

✅ DFDL types = XML Schema types
✅ IIB internally converts them → ESQL types
✅ INTERVAL & BIT not supported
✅ Constraints (e.g., xs:nonNegativeInteger) auto-validate data
✅ Importers (COBOL / C) auto-map correct DFDL types


